---
description: graphify knowledge graph context
alwaysApply: true
---

This project may have a graphify knowledge graph at `graphify-out/`.

**When `graphify-out/graph.json` exists and `graphify` is on PATH**, prefer graphify before broad exploration:

- `graphify query "<question>"` — scoped subgraph for codebase or architecture questions
- `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"` — dependency path between two symbols
- `graphify explain "<concept>"` — nodes related to a concept

If `graphify-out/graph.json` does **not** exist yet, use normal Read/Grep/Glob and run `graphify .` when you need the graph.

- If `graphify-out/wiki/index.md` exists, navigate it instead of reading raw files
- Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` only for broad architecture review when query/path/explain are insufficient; it may be stale until `graphify update .` runs
- After modifying code files, run `graphify update .` to keep the graph current (AST-only, no API cost)
